  "_comment": "Default-deny (EPERM) seccomp whitelist for OJ judge containers. The allow list is the empirical union of every syscall observed while compiling AND running all supported judge languages (C/C++ via ccache, Rust, Go, asm, Java, Kotlin, Python, Node, Ruby), including ojrun/GNU-time wrappers, tini, coreutils timeout, the interactive FIFO wrapper and the pool sanitiser; a small set of safe family-companion syscalls is added on top. Extend the list only after re-tracing with `strace -f` (plain, no class filters) under the production container flags. amd64/x32 only (judge images are amd64).",
